  <h2 class="section">What I do</h2>
  <div class="section-rule"></div>

  <div class="funcs">
    <div class="fn"><b>Leadership.</b> <span>Grew from founding scientist to a team of more than fifteen, including managers and senior ICs; own AI strategy, product leadership, and the client-, investor-, partner-, and competitor-facing work.</span></div>
    <div class="fn"><b>Agents &amp; post-training.</b> <span>Post-training (SFT, PEFT/QLoRA, and verifiable-reward RL), agentic systems, evaluation, and inference optimization; for example, a 4B model post-trained to cut errors roughly 50% versus GPT-5.2 at nearly 20&times; lower inference cost.</span></div>
    <div class="fn"><b>Legal AI.</b> <span>Seven years building systems that read legal demands and draft grounded objections, two of the startups since acquired; provide hands-on technical mentorship while doing the IC work myself.</span></div>
    <div class="fn"><b>Risk intelligence.</b> <span>Lead RiskWise, an agentic system that surfaces latent and emerging risks; its verifiable-reward agents produce signals that predict multidistrict litigation at 0.90 held-out AUC (2025).</span></div>
    <div class="fn"><b>Predictive modeling &amp; forecasting.</b> <span>Built early AI-assisted forecasting in 2023, using RAG for covariate search (Generative Predictor Search cut MAPE 15.6% while running 13&times; faster), plus Bayesian pipelines and predictive forecasting across financial services and consumer goods.</span></div>
    <div class="fn"><b>AI for science.</b> <span>First author on NEO, featured by NVIDIA, and co-author on a Nature Portfolio paper; now building agents for scientific discovery and deep-learning research.</span></div>
  </div>

  <h2 class="section">Selected work</h2>
  <div class="section-rule"></div>

  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-thumb-wrap">
        <img class="card-thumb" src="assets/img/blog-harness.png" alt="Risk harness architecture diagram">
      </div>
      <div class="card-body">
        <div class="card-kicker">Agent infrastructure</div>
        <h3><a href="blog/risk-harness.html">The Agent Risk Harness</a></h3>
        <p>The memory, procedures, permissions, and decision traces an agent needs before you can
          put a real decision through it.</p>
        <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag">agents</span><span class="tag">infrastructure</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-thumb-wrap">
        <img class="card-thumb" src="assets/img/mdl-loop-thumb.jpg"
             alt="Diagram of a Thompson-sampling bandit allocating research agents under a code-computed verifiable reward">
      </div>
      <div class="card-body">
        <div class="card-kicker">Bandit-driven agentic search and verifiable rewards</div>
        <h3><a href="projects/mdl-litigation-prediction.html">Verifiable Rewards for Predicting Multidistrict Litigation</a></h3>
        <p>A Thompson-sampling bandit allocates research agents under a reward computed in code,
          feeding a discrete-time hazard model. 0.90 held-out AUC.</p>
        <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag">bandits</span><span class="tag">verifiable rewards</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-thumb-wrap">
        <img class="card-thumb" src="assets/img/blog-gps.png" alt="Win rate comparison for LLM-driven forecasting">
      </div>
      <div class="card-body">
        <div class="card-kicker">LLM reasoning</div>
        <h3><a href="blog/generative-predictor-search.html">Generative Predictor Search</a></h3>
        <p>LLM reasoning proposes and validates covariates for time-series forecasting, cutting
          MAPE 15.6% and running 13&times; faster than exhaustive search.</p>
        <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag">llm</span><span class="tag">forecasting</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-thumb-wrap">
        <img class="card-thumb" src="https://samuelhkahn.github.io/neo-paper/images/good_image_cutouts.png"
             alt="Ground-based, space-based, and super-resolved galaxy image triplets">
      </div>
      <div class="card-body">
        <div class="card-kicker">Generative models</div>
        <h3><a href="https://samuelhkahn.github.io/neo-paper/">NEO: Photometric Super-Resolution</a></h3>
        <p>A conditional GAN that recovers measurement structure ground-based seeing destroys,
          improving accuracy by factors of 2 to 10. Featured by NVIDIA.</p>
        <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag">cGAN</span><span class="tag">imaging</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-thumb-wrap">
        <img class="card-thumb" src="assets/img/blog-thinking.png" alt="Entity-level risk attribution accuracy: RiskWise-4B ahead of GPT-4o and GPT-4o-mini">
      </div>
      <div class="card-body">
        <div class="card-kicker">Model post-training</div>
        <h3><a href="blog/thinking-without-thinking.html">Whispers of Latent Reasoning</a></h3>
        <p>A 4B thinking-tuned model beats GPT-5.2 on entity-level risk attribution and keeps the
          gains even with chain-of-thought suppressed.</p>
        <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag">post-training</span><span class="tag">reasoning</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-thumb-wrap">
        <img class="card-thumb" src="assets/img/agentic-network.png"
             alt="Albedo climate network with hubs concentrated in the tropical Pacific">
      </div>
      <div class="card-body">
        <div class="card-kicker">Autonomous research</div>
        <h3><a href="projects/agentic-discovery-climate.html">Agentic Discovery for Science</a></h3>
        <p>19 cycles and 49 analyses on 25 years of satellite data, with every finding put
          through an adversarial gate before it was kept.</p>
        <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag">agents</span><span class="tag">MCTS</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

